# Code owners for this repository.
#
# GitHub uses this file together with the "Require review from Code Owners"
# branch-protection rule on `main` to decide who must approve a pull request
# before it can merge (including via auto-merge).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Design intent
#
#   Non-docs PRs -> human approval required (@thomas3650).
#   Docs-only PRs -> no human approval required. They merge automatically
#                    once the Docs Auto-Merge workflow arms auto-merge AND
#                    the required status checks (`build-test`,
#                    `copilot-review-clean`) turn green.
#
#   `copilot-review-clean` is posted by .github/workflows/copilot-review-gate.yml
#   and turns green only when GitHub Copilot code review has reviewed the
#   current head commit with no unresolved inline comments and no
#   CHANGES_REQUESTED. That's how Copilot's review effectively gates the
#   docs auto-merge path without CODEOWNERS having to treat Copilot as an
#   approver (Copilot code review only ever submits state=COMMENTED, as
#   verified empirically on PR #23).
#
# CODEOWNERS mechanics
#
#   The catch-all rule below assigns @thomas3650 as code owner of every
#   path in the repo. The explicit "docs/**" rule immediately below it has
#   NO owners, which per GitHub's CODEOWNERS syntax clears the catch-all
#   for docs paths -- meaning docs-only PRs have no code owner and, with
#   `require_code_owner_review: true`, need no code-owner approval to
#   merge.
#
#   Order matters: last matching rule wins. Keep `/docs/**` after `*`.
#
# Prerequisite (out-of-band repo config, not versionable here)
#
#   Ruleset on `main` must have:
#     * "Require a pull request before merging" enabled
#     * "Require review from Code Owners"        enabled
#     * "Required approvals" = 0
#       (Approvals are gated by CODEOWNERS per-path, not a global count.)
#     * Required status checks include `build-test` and
#       `copilot-review-clean`.
#
#   Without those rules this file has no effect.

# Catch-all: everything not otherwise matched needs @thomas3650 approval.
*         @thomas3650

# docs/** intentionally has NO code owner. With
# `require_code_owner_review: true` and `required_approvals: 0`, this
# lets docs-only PRs merge without a human approval, gated only by the
# required status checks (`build-test`, `copilot-review-clean`) and the
# eligibility logic in .github/workflows/docs-auto-merge.yml.
/docs/**
